  "raw_text": "Step 1: Substitute \\(x = 4\\) into the expression \\((3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x+1\\).\n\nStep 2: Calculate each part of the expression separately.\n- For \\((3x-2)\\), substitute \\(x = 4\\):\n  \\[\n  3(4) - 2 = 12 - 2 = 10\n  \\]\n- For \\((4x+1)\\), substitute \\(x = 4\\):\n  \\[\n  4(4) + 1 = 16 + 1 = 17\n  \\]\n- For \\((3x-2)4x\\), substitute \\(x = 4\\):\n  \\[\n  (3(4) - 2)4(4) = 10 \\cdot 16 = 160\n  \\]\n\nStep 3: Substitute these values back into the original expression:\n\\[\n(10)(17) - 160 + 1\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Perform the multiplication and addition/subtraction:\n\\[\n170 - 160 + 1 = 11\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{11}<|im_end|>",
